meta {
  name: PDF to Images
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/forms/pdfengines/convert
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/zip
}

body:multipart-form {
  files[]: @file(./sample.pdf)
  pdfFormat: PDF/A-1a
}

docs {
  # PDF to Images

  Converts a PDF file to images using Gotenberg's PDF engines.

  ## Endpoint

  `POST /forms/pdfengines/convert`

  ## Form Fields

  | Field       | Type   | Required | Description                                      |
  |-------------|--------|----------|--------------------------------------------------|
  | files[]     | file   | Yes      | One or more PDF files to convert                 |
  | pdfFormat   | string | No       | Output PDF format (e.g., PDF/A-1a, PDF/A-2b)     |

  ## Response

  Returns a ZIP archive containing the converted files when multiple files
  are submitted, or a single file if only one file is provided.

  ## Notes

  - Supported PDF formats: `PDF/A-1a`, `PDF/A-2b`, `PDF/A-3b`
  - The conversion relies on the available PDF engines (e.g., LibreOffice, pdfcpu)
  - Ensure the input PDF is not password-protected
}
